#hasheq((content-digest . "1790df4e137262d86d8432d6513bccbcb477ead0a12b78f660909e5045937965") (milestone . 896) (plan-id . "fb67e0429ed155a4b4e3f31afe3ef3ca7748ee891c06247b11e5e2a86cfebd75") (report . "Twenty-one independent review rounds against the frozen W5 wave doc, ending with R21 APPROVED at this exact head. R1 found three defects (nested provenance fields disabled by non-matching ancestor keys; the F13 restore could not restore a stale PLAN.md; a legacy manifest hash broken by a trailing empty element). R2 refused a non-reproducible matrix recorded head. R3 refused an unbound tree/digest gap; R4 a non-canonical current-wave SHA256SUMS. R5 refused timing values from unrelated numeric fields and an uncaught exception on malformed SUMS lines. R6/R7 refused non-recursive JSON coverage. R8 refused the missing F7 register guard, unverified recorded sha256 fields, and the intra-JSON-only cross-artifact check. R9 refused tree fields walked as commits, a subtractive timing set, and non-Python-compatible canonical escapes. R10 refused an order-dependent report scan and one-level artifact discovery. R11 refused branch-dependent gate strictness and a crash on directory-relative current-wave SUMS entries. R12 refused discovery that did not implement the documented artifacts/**/v*/ scope. R13 required exact head binding for head-claiming fields while keeping ancestor semantics for pinned observation heads. R14 found no blocking defect. R15 refused the shallow-checkout skip that left CI green without exercising the real tree and the fail-open constrained path. R16 refused JSON null canonicalized as a quoted string. R17 refused a declared current wave that could pass with no artifact directory. R18 APPROVED at 280835b3a and required rebinding the record at the final head. R19 required the one-tag-per-line metadata fix so the schema-1 tier matrix tracks the new family (both tier matrices regenerated) and asked for the final-commit regeneration to be recorded. R20 APPROVED at 3795a9803 and required the stale area ownership map to be regenerated before the record commit, plus the tier-matrix check in the validation record. R21 verified and APPROVED the ownership-map regeneration at this head. The review series is the compensating control for the post-R18 governance-sync commits (0d7534381, 037c85d23, 3795a9803, 8f534785b). One structural recommendation is recorded, not blocking: the area ownership map has no drift gate (the tier matrix has --ownership-map --check plus the milestone-gate family check), so it silently drifted from W0 through W4; a byte-identity or digest gate is recommended as follow-up work. Every accepted item is documented in docs/reports/ARTIFACT-PROVENANCE-v1.00.31.md; the lint reports 941 historical provenance notes and zero drift at this head.") (reviewed-sha . "8f534785bef1465e679741cb8e92415733ba5782") (reviewer . "pi-reviewer-subagent:readonly-w5-impl-review-r21:campaign-v1.00.31-w5-4a19d60b4:2026-09-23") (schema-version . 2) (scope . "W5 artifact provenance and determinism: scripts/ci/verify-artifact-provenance.rkt (SHA256SUMS binding with recursive coverage and both historical spellings plus typed refusal for a directory-relative current entry, provenance heads with exact binding for head-claiming fields and ancestor semantics for pinned observation heads, paired tree validation, canonical JSON byte-compatible with Python json.dumps(ensure_ascii=True) including the JSON null symbol, cross-artifact prose/structured timing agreement across bound markdown reports against the complete per-version timing union, recorded-digest-to-file verification, recursive discovery over artifacts/**/v*, and a declared current wave that must exist), the coordinator artifact-provenance gate with branch-independent current-wave derivation (extensions/gsd/delivery-coordinator.rkt), the F7 register guard (tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt), the CI workflow shard's full-history checkout (.github/workflows/ci.yml), tests/test-artifact-provenance.rkt (26 tests, one-tag-per-line metadata with an explicit unit boundary), the deterministic generator and bound artifacts under artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w5/, the regenerated tier-ownership matrices (artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.29-w0/ownership-matrix.json + SHA256SUMS, tests/tier-ownership-matrix.json) and the regenerated area ownership map (reports/test-ownership-map.{md,json}), docs/reports/ARTIFACT-PROVENANCE-v1.00.31.md, and the F13 frozen-contract staleness guard in extensions/gsd/{plan-snapshot,campaign-state,campaign-repository}.rkt at implementation head 8f534785bef1465e679741cb8e92415733ba5782 with content digest 1790df4e137262d86d8432d6513bccbcb477ead0a12b78f660909e5045937965.") (timestamp . "2026-09-23T00:00:00Z") (verdict . "APPROVED") (wave . "W5"))
